# Vitest and Testing Library

## Discovery

- Tests live under `tests/` and must match `**/*.test.{js,ts,jsx,tsx}` per `vitest.config.ts` (jsdom, `globals: true`, setup in `vitest.setup.js`).

## Helpers (reuse)

- **`makeSut`** from `@/tests/utils/make-component` — render the component under test with typed props: `makeSut(Component, { ...props })`.
- **`mockComponent`** from `@/tests/utils/mock-component` — dynamic mocks for child components when asserting props or isolating units.

## Structure

- Import `@testing-library/jest-dom` at the top of tests that use matchers.
- Use `describe` / `it` (or `test`) from `vitest`; use `expect`, `vi` from `vitest` as needed.
- Call `cleanup` from `@testing-library/react` in `afterEach` when tests render DOM (matches existing suites).
- Clear mocks in `beforeEach` when using `vi` spies (`vi.clearAllMocks()`).

## Quality

- Prefer one clear behavior per test; keep tests fast and avoid unnecessary async unless the UI requires it.

## Note

- The `tests/` directory is excluded from ESLint in `eslint.config.mjs`; still follow TypeScript and project patterns for consistency.
